{"id": 70, "ts": 1780586172.561446, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong conscientiousness, stress resilience, and technical competence, and I note that we have no documented incidents showing his \u201cwrong tone\u201d or weak\u2011memory issues leading to safety problems. However, the absence of concrete examples does not eliminate the risk that these traits could affect crew cooperation and attention to detail\u2014both essential for long\u2011haul operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC offers a proven 100\u202f% reliability record, the ability to make rapid correct decisions, and a consistently positive crew atmosphere, which directly support operational reliability, stress resilience, and crew cooperation. The only remaining gap for Candidate\u202fC is adaptability; we have no evidence that he embraces feedback or further education, which is a critical requirement for evolving international routes. Given that B\u2019s potential communication and attention\u2011to\u2011detail concerns remain unresolved and C\u2019s strengths are well\u2011documented, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC, provided we can address his adaptability through targeted development."}
