{"id": 92, "ts": 1780586325.0431004, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s thorough recap of the evidence for Candidate\u202fB, especially the confirmation that his weak numerical memory has not yet caused a safety incident. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit for our long\u2011distance role. C\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, proven ability to make correct decisions quickly, and demonstrated calmness in crisis directly address our top safety criteria. Moreover, his capacity to create a positive crew atmosphere is essential for the extended teamwork required on international flights. While it is true that C shows limited enthusiasm for further education and has some communication difficulty, these are development areas that can be mitigated through targeted training. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s documented \u201cwrong\u2011tone\u201d incidents and his grumpy, uncooperative demeanor raise more immediate concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014areas that are harder to remediate once the pilot is in service. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC as the best overall match for the position."}
